2026-07-28 14:16:26,268 - rag_service.services.generation_service - INFO - {"event": "rag_query_trace", "query": "How is CRP used for stratification?", "retrieved_chunks": [], "context_char_count": 0, "response": "## CRP Use for Stratification in the Protocol\n\n### Original Protocol Version (Version 1.0)\nIn the original protocol, CRP was used as a **stratification factor for randomisation**. Specifically, patients were stratified by **elevated (\u22653 mg/L) CRP levels** as one of the randomisation stratification criteria (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p92).\n\n### Updated Protocol Version (Version 1.1)\nHowever, this was **changed in Protocol Version 1.1**. The stratification by CRP levels was **removed**, and randomisation stratification was updated to be based instead on:\n- **Prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no)**, and\n- **Consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no)**\n\nThis change is confirmed in both the Randomisation section and the Primary Endpoint analysis section (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p36; p68).\n\n### CRP as an Exploratory Biomarker\nAlthough CRP is no longer a stratification factor, it continues to play a role in the study as an **exploratory biomarker**. Change from Baseline to Weeks 4, 8, and 12 in CRP is measured as an exploratory endpoint (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p25), and CRP is analysed **locally at investigational sites** (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p45).\n\nAdditionally, patients are split into **subgroups based on baseline IL-6/sIL-6R complex levels** (not CRP) for exploratory subgroup analyses (Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf, p13).", "sources": [{"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 92, "section": "Appendix 4 - Summary of Changes for Version 1.1", "exactText": "90 patients will be centrally, dynamically, stratified randomly (by elevated ( \u22653 mg/L) CRP levels, and stable conventional treatment (prior treatment with amino salicylates, corticosteroids, and immunosuppressive drugs)) assigned to 3 groups (1:1:1) to receive 600mg TJ301 biweekly (Q2W), 300mg TJ301 Q2W or placebo Q2W.", "bboxes": [[52.59044647216797, 495.76949310302734, 771.7723999023438, 121.96722412109375]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 36, "section": "4.2.2 Randomisation", "exactText": "Randomisation will be stratified by prior corticosteroids treatment (yes/no) and consent to participate in PK substudy (yes/no).", "bboxes": [[72.0, 233.90398291015606, 538.44, 178.01497521784836]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 68, "section": "9.6.2 Primary Endpoint", "exactText": "This binary outcome (remission status=yes/no) variable will be analysed by a logistic regression model with treatment and the randomisation-stratification factors (prior corticosteroids treatment and consent to participate in PK substudy) as fixed effects and the baseline full Mayo score as covariate.", "bboxes": [[71.99999999999997, 721.7039829101564, 558.8399999999996, 605.2149752178486]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 25, "section": "Exploratory Endpoints", "exactText": "Change from Baseline to Weeks 4, 8, and 12 in exploratory biomarkers (erythrocyte sedimentation rate [ESR], C-reactive protein (CRP), IL-6, IL-6/sIL-6R complex, neutrophil and platelet count, faecal calprotectin).", "bboxes": [[89.88, 589.7999829101561, 550.68, 548.5749752178484]], "relevance": "high"}, {"name": "Protocol_Ulcerative Colitis.pdf", "page": 45, "section": "Table 1 Time and Events Schedule", "exactText": "Biomarkers erythrocyte sedimentation rate [ESR], C-reactive protein (CRP), neutrophil and platelet count tests will be analysed in local sites.", "bboxes": [[77.15952000000003, 132.16128732421873, 795.356639999999, 115.30609217037261]], "relevance": "high"}], "timing": {"response_cache_hit": false, "semantic_cache_hit": true, "chunks_compressed": false, "embedding_ms": 1447.7760840090923, "embedding_cache_hit